ance of your surrogate by your fertility center If there is medical need or other reasons why a new surrogate is required, these services are provided again. Backing Our Proven Process: Up to $7,500 Credit for Rematching We believe in our proven process so strongly that we back it with confidence. ConceiveAbilities will defray the medical screening costs charged by your fertility clinic for rematching, giving you confidence in our surrogates and peace of mind during the process. In the event a surrogate is disqualified or withdraws, intended parents will receive a $2,500 credit after a first failed medical screening and $5,000 after a first failed embryo transfer, at rematch, ensuring your journey continues smoothly with a new match. Please note that you, as an intended parent, are responsible for all bills and expenses associated with your fertility clinic. Your All-In package includes recruiting, screening, and matching you with a healthy and highly qualified surrogate and includes unlimited rematches. Legal Expenses Provision for the legal services you will need for your journey is included. Our legal team is the best in the industry. Their expertise and guidance is a part of the All-In Package. Legal representation for your surrogate; and the proper establishment of your parentage rights. These services are provided through the network of attorneys that ConceiveAbilities has vetted for their surrogacy expertise. Organizing an effective partnership with your surrogate. Once you have your surrogate match, we create a surrogacy agreement or surrogacy contract between both the surrogate and intended parents, which outlines fair involvement between both parties throughout the surrogacy journey. For instance, the agreement ensures the intended parents will be active participants through the surrogate’s prenatal care and beyond. Coordinating the legal and escrow work required to receive clearance from your fertility center for embryo transfer, inclusive of drafting and